# The attic of Death House: the toy chest (the children's remains), the dollhouse (which shows the secret stair) and
# the hidden panel in the storage room's corner (book area 18). Every way of finding the stair runs through
# secret_stair, which grants the level 2 milestone exactly once. Also the nursemaid's remains in the storage trunk.

~ toy_chest
narrate examine:toy_chest
if flag.death_house_children_remains_taken
  Narrator: The chest is empty now, except for a wooden horse with one ear and a faint smell of lavender.
  -> END
endif
Narrator: Under the dolls and the wooden horse lie two small bundles wrapped in faded blankets, tied shut with a child's careful knot.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Oh, little ones. You waited such a long time.
if not name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject species:dwarf: Small bones. The small ones always weigh the most.
endif
-> chest_choice

~ chest_choice
* [Medicine DC 10] Learn how they died. -> chest_medicine | chest_medicine_fail
* Gather the bones and carry them with you. -> chest_take
* Close the lid. -> END

~ chest_medicine
Narrator: No wounds, no breaks: just bones too light for their size, curled the way children curl when they fall asleep hungry and cold. Nobody killed them; somebody forgot them.
if not flag.death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:thistle: Shut in and left. Worst thing there is.
-> chest_choice

~ chest_medicine_fail
Narrator: Old bones in old blankets. Whatever happened to them, it happened a long time ago.
-> chest_choice

~ chest_take
set death_house_children_remains_taken
quest rose_and_thorn remains
Narrator: The bundles weigh almost nothing. Whoever carries them will feel them all the way down.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'll carry them. Gently. They'll not feel a single bump, I promise.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I've carried a lot of things to market. Never anything this light. Or this heavy.
-> END

~ dollhouse
narrate examine:dollhouse
Narrator: It is this house, perfect down to the doorknobs: the hall, the den with its tiny stag's head, the nursery with its tiny crib. Someone spent years on it.
* [Investigation DC 12] Go over it room by room. -> doll_close | doll_quick
* [if flag.death_house_children_met and not flag.death_house_children_riding and not flag.death_house_children_at_rest] Ask Rose what it shows. -> doll_rose
* Leave it be. -> END

~ doll_close
Narrator: In the corner of the little attic storage room, a panel no bigger than a fingernail hides a stair that winds down inside the walls, past every floor, below a cellar the house doesn't have.
Narrator: At the bottom is a room with a tiny stone table, and beside it a lump of grey clay, shaped like a sleeping heap.
if not flag.death_house_dollhouse_altar_seen
  set death_house_dollhouse_altar_seen
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:ratatoille: Accurate to the doorknobs, secret stair and all. This is not a toy. It is a map someone was too guilty to burn.
if not name:ratatoille
  interject tag:scholarly: Someone put the truth in a toy, where only a child would look. That's a confession.
endif
-> secret_stair

~ doll_quick
Narrator: It takes {name} a while, but there it is: in the corner of the toy storage room, a panel no bigger than a fingernail, and a stair inside the walls.
-> secret_stair

~ doll_rose
Rose: Father made it for my birthday. He made it too well. It even has the stair they use at night. I found it with a hairpin.
Thorn: She showed me. I wasn't supposed to know.
Narrator: Rose's finger touches a panel in the corner of the toy storage room. It swings open on a staircase winding down inside the walls.
-> secret_stair

~ secret_panel
narrate search:storage_panel
Narrator: The seam runs in a neat rectangle. Pressed, the plaster swings inward on a breath of warm air, onto a stair that winds down inside the walls.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Hinges on the inside. Lovely work. I used to know people who'd pay good money for a door like this.
if not name:wren_featherfoot
  interject class:rogue: Hinges on the inside. Whoever built this didn't want to be followed.
endif
-> secret_stair

~ secret_stair
if not flag.death_house_secret_stair_found
  set death_house_secret_stair_found
  quest death_house secret_stair
  Narrator: In the storage room, the bare nook in the corner is not bare anymore. A stair waits behind it, going down.
endif
-> milestone

~ milestone
if not flag.death_house_milestone_dungeon
  set death_house_milestone_dungeon
  xp milestone
  Narrator: You have come farther into this house than most guests, and it has noticed. So have you.
endif
-> END

~ nursemaid_trunk
narrate examine:nursemaid_trunk
Narrator: Under the dust sheet, a big traveling trunk. Inside, wrapped in a bedsheet gone stiff and brown, lie the bones of a young woman, a faded blue ribbon still tied in her hair.
if flag.death_house_learned_walter
  Narrator: Walter's nurse. They didn't let her go far.
endif
* [Medicine DC 10] Learn how she died. -> trunk_medicine | trunk_medicine_fail
* Close the lid gently. -> END

~ trunk_medicine
Narrator: Stab wounds, many of them, the blade turned on the ribs again and again. Someone did this in a fury, and then folded her neatly into a trunk.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Angry first, then tidy after. I've met that sort. They smile at you in church.
if not name:godrick_pendlebrook
  interject class:cleric: Whoever did this was angry, and then very, very calm. I'll pray for her twice.
endif
-> END

~ trunk_medicine_fail
Narrator: Old bones in an old sheet. The sheet tells the story better than you can.
-> END
